e if Rogers stumbles.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Neal Dunn (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Florida's 2nd District is an open seat after Republican Neal Dunn's retirement, and it remains deeply favorable ground for the GOP with a partisan lean of about eight points Republican. Austin Rogers won a contested primary in August and enters the general election with a large financial edge: roughly $1 million raised, $387,000 in the bank, and about $1.4 million in outside support, including a U.S. Chamber endorsement. Democrat Amanda Green has raised about $348,000 but reported only about $28,000 on hand.\n\nRatings from most analysts place the district in the safe or solid Republican column, with a few calling it likely or leaning Republican, and prediction markets give Rogers roughly a 93 percent chance. No credible head-to-head general-election polling is available, so uncertainty is somewhat elevated, but the combination of district lean, money, and outside consensus points to a Republican hold.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0837, "margin": -8.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.084, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1162, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1045, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0789, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0848, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1006, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0806, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0753, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0679, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0619, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0853, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0683, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0534, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0699, "margin": -10.